---
title: Spiced lamb tacos
tags: [mexican, lamb]
cuisine: mexican
source: Lamb Taco by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/lamb-taco
---

== Morita salsa ==

Toast the @morita chiles{4}(stemmed, seeded) in a #sauté pan{} over medium heat until fragrant. Take off the heat, cover with @water{} and soak ~{10%minutes}. Drain, keeping the liquid.

Blend the chiles with the @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), @onion{1/2}(diced), @roasted tomatillos{1/2%cup}, @roasted tomatoes{1/2%cup} and @apple cider vinegar{1%tbsp} in a #blender{} until smooth, adding soaking liquid to loosen. Refrigerate.

== Cucumber pico de gallo ==

Mix the @cucumbers{1%cup}(diced), @white onion{1/4%cup}(diced), @cilantro{2%tbsp}(chopped), @jalapenos{1%tbsp}(minced), @salt{1/2%tsp} and the juice of @lime{1}. Refrigerate.

== Tahini crema ==

Whisk the @tahini{1/2%cup} with @water{1/4%cup}(warm), then whisk in the @sour cream{1%cup}, @lime juice{2%tbsp}, @salt{1/2%tsp} and @garlic{1%clove}(grated). Refrigerate.

== Lamb ==

Heat a little @neutral oil{} in a #sauté pan{} over medium-high heat. Add the @ground lamb shoulder{2%lb} and brown it, breaking it up with a #wooden spoon{}.

Season with the @ground cumin{2%tbsp}, @kosher salt{1%tbsp}, @ground black pepper{2%tsp}, @ancho chile powder{1%tsp}, @pasilla chile powder{1%tsp} and @ground coriander{1%tsp}.

Cook ~{8%minutes}, stirring now and then, until browned and 160°F inside. Pour off the fat and keep warm over low heat.

== Assembly ==

Lay out the @corn tortillas{}(heirloom). Top each with 3 oz of the lamb, 1 tbsp of the salsa and 1 tbsp of the pico de gallo. Drizzle with the crema and finish with @cilantro{}(leaves).

> The lamb makes about 36 oz cooked, enough for 12 tacos.
